From: numbereleven-a
Subject: [PATCH] sftp: skip the request id in a symlink STATUS reply

The CVE-2025-15661 backport reads the first u32 after the packet type of an
SSH_FXP_STATUS reply as the status code, but that u32 is the request id; the
code follows it. A failed readlink/realpath set last_errno to the request
id, and with an id of 0 reported success without filling the target.
---
diff --git a/src/sftp.c b/src/sftp.c
index 72d0c00..50ef644 100644
--- a/src/sftp.c
+++ b/src/sftp.c
@@ -3941,7 +3941,9 @@ static int sftp_symlink(LIBSSH2_SFTP *sftp, const char *path,
     }
 
     if(packet_type == SSH_FXP_STATUS) {
-        if(_libssh2_get_u32(&buf, &tmp_u32)) {
+        /* the request id comes first, then the status code */
+        if(_libssh2_get_u32(&buf, &tmp_u32) ||
+           _libssh2_get_u32(&buf, &tmp_u32)) {
             LIBSSH2_FREE(session, data);
             return _libssh2_error(session, LIBSSH2_ERROR_SFTP_PROTOCOL,
                                   "SFTP Protocol Error (code)");
